<title>USA: Pilots union pleased by UPS deal.</title>
<headline>Pilots union pleased by UPS deal.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The union representing pilots at United Parcel Service said it was pleased that the Teamsters union had reached agreement with the firm to effectively end a 15-day strike.</p>
<p>&quot;The Independent Pilots Association is delighted that the International Brotherhood of Teamsters and UPS have reached a tentative agreement,&quot; the pilots group said in a statement.</p>
<p>The Kentucky-based IPA, which holds its own talks next month with UPS over pilots' contracts, said it has requested a meeting with UPS officials to draw up a return-to-work plan once the Teamsters strike has officially ended.</p>
<p>IPA pilots refused to work at UPS during the Teamsters strike.</p>
<p>((Washington newsroom, 202 898-8300))</p>
</text>
